      "message": "I\u0027m just lamenting that we still have a mix of the C and C++ names for these headers: string.h vs. cstring, stdlib.h vs. cstdlib, throughout our code. We should prefer the C++ versions, and I was hoping that IWYU would push us in that direction, but from this CL, I see it updating includes to use both forms.\n\nThe main distinction is that the .h versions put things in the global namespace, and the cxxx versions put them in std:: (though some toolchains appear to also put them in global namespace). I was just trying to figure out how we encourage IWYU to favor the cxxx versions.\n\nBut we\u0027re still no worse off than we are today, so not a huge deal.",
